  "teamTimelineForkTitle": "Early client development",
  "teamTimelineForkBody": "Early test versions helped define the Android runtime, subscription handling, diagnostics, and interface that Etonify now maintains.",
  "teamTimelineRefactorTitle": "Large refactor",
  "teamTimelineRefactorBody": "We gradually split the large legacy code into focused components, simplified VPN control, and added checks for critical scenarios.",
  "teamTimelineCoreTitle": "Moving to etonify-core",
  "teamTimelineCoreBody": "After MeowSingBox, the client moved to a more stable sing-box base with the changes Etonify needs. Maintaining our own core makes updates and testing easier, while URLTest, server failover, and resource-cleanup improvements benefit everyday use.",
  "teamTimelineNowTitle": "Etonify today",
  "teamTimelineNowBody": "Etonify is still evolving: we keep simplifying UX, improving Android stability, and cutting technical debt without losing the speed-focused VPN experience.",
